  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "[Security]\n            - Hardened chunked transfer encoding against DoS: chunk size parsing now uses TryParse with non-negative\n            validation to prevent malicious peers from triggering excessive memory allocation\n            - Added non-negative validation for parsed Content-Length headers in both request and response\n            deserializers\n            - Added ObjectDisposedException guard in ArgusClient.SendAsync to fail fast after disposal\n            - Fixed resource leak in ArgusClient.SendAsync: StreamWriter and StreamReader are now properly disposed\n            with leaveOpen: true\n\n            [Performance]\n            - Replaced Substring().Trim() with AsSpan().Trim().ToString() in header parsing hot paths to reduce\n            intermediate string allocations\n            - Replaced ContainsKey + indexer double lookup with TryGetValue in ArgusBodySerializerRegistry\n            - Cached JsonSerializerOptions instance in SampleClientService instead of allocating per call\n            - Used ReadAsync(Memory byte) overload instead of inexact Read(byte[], int, int) in chunked encoding\n\n            [Refactoring]\n            - Introduced ArgusHeaderNames constants (Accept, ContentType, ContentLength, CorrelationToken, Timestamp)\n            replacing all string literals\n            - Reordered IArgusClient and ArgusClient method overloads to be adjacent by name\n            - Reordered ArgusResponseSerializer so all Write overloads are grouped, followed by all WriteAsync\n            overloads\n            - Refactored GuidExtensions.FromShortGuidArray to use a private iterator method\n            - Refactored ArgusClient.SendAsync to use requestSerializer.WriteAsync",
